    "body": "## Summary\n\nIn the gRPC chat streaming path (`process_streaming_chunks`), the prompt token count is inflated by a factor of `n` whenever `n > 1`.\n\nEach choice's `Complete` message stores the **shared** prompt length into `prompt_tokens[index]`:\n\n```rust\nprompt_tokens.insert(index, complete.prompt_tokens() as u32);\n```\n\nThe prompt is prefilled once and reused across all `n` choices, so every index holds the *same* value. The usage chunk and the streaming metrics then did:\n\n```rust\nlet total_prompt: u32 = prompt_tokens.values().sum();\n```\n\nwhich adds the shared prompt once per choice → `usage.prompt_tokens`, `total_tokens`, and the `input_tokens` metric are all reported as `prompt × n`.\n\n## Fix\n\nAggregate the prompt with a small helper that takes the shared value (`max`) so the prompt is counted exactly once:\n\n```rust\nfn aggregate_prompt_tokens(prompt_tokens: &HashMap<u32, u32>) -> u32 {\n    prompt_tokens.values().copied().max().unwrap_or(0)\n}\n```\n\nApplied at both sites (usage chunk + metrics). Completion tokens stay summed (`.values().sum()`), since those legitimately differ per choice. Behavior for `n = 1` is unchanged (`sum == max`).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New `#[cfg(test)]` unit tests for `aggregate_prompt_tokens`:\n  - `prompt_tokens_counted_once_for_n_choices`: `{0:100, 1:100, 2:100}` → `100` (not `300`)\n  - `prompt_tokens_single_choice_unchanged`: `{0:42}` → `42`\n  - `prompt_tokens_empty_is_zero`: `{}` → `0`\n- [x] Confirmed `cargo` isn't required to see the bug: the pre-fix `sum()` yields `300` for an `n=3` shared-100-token prompt; the helper yields `100`.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #29631787506](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/29631787506)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #29631787481](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/29631787481)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
